A||||13||V8Dreamer||Thoughts on Cutting springs.....||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||09-07-2001||04:55 PM||||Just wondering if anyone here has done it....if you're against it, I already did it, so there's no need to tell me not to, I just wanted to talk to some other people to see what they think of the handling and advantages/disadvantages compared to stock or lowering springs.  My GT just feels very unpredictable and bouncy...I'm not sure if the handling got worse or better...could be partly due to a possibly piss poor alignment too.  Anyway, I took 1.5 coils off the rear and 2 coils off the front.  Any comments welcome!<P>Thanks,<BR>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||09-07-2001||05:53 PM||||in a word ....dont. Some people have done it, but its far better to save a little and buy lowered springs. When you cut some off, you affect the spring rate and can get some wierd handling.||||reg||1
Z||000002||California Kid||09-07-2001||05:59 PM||||That sounds like a pretty drastic chop!!! Just curious how much the body lowered from the original stock height???<P>My 88 springs were cut to lower both front and rear "body" 1 1/2 inch. Koni's and urethane bushings at all corners, 4 wheel alignment set for road course. Car handling is "out of this world".||||reg||1
Z||000003||MrPBody||09-07-2001||08:41 PM||||I cut my '85 SE's WS6 springs 1 coil in front and 1/2 coil in rear.  I'm pretty happy with the result.  The ride is stiffer, for sure; I don't think I will cut mine further.<P>Good alignment can make a big difference, as can better shocks.<P>How would you describe your handling problems?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||AL||09-07-2001||09:01 PM||||i was just thinking, who makes lowered springs for the fiero? and which ones are painted blue? the reason i ask, i took these off a gt at the junkyard and i want to know if these are some kind of name brand or if the owner painted them.<BR><B>AL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <BR>84 Indy 4 speed(stole it) powered mirrors and windows<BR>leather seats,over the head scoop,stereo.<BR>86 GT<BR>ported and polished heads,ported manifolds, 80 series flowmaster,K&N air filter,holley side scoop,decklid scoop, rear swaybar,sub system(stock) powered mirrors and windows.new shoks and struts.<BR>89 WS6 GTA 5.7L<BR>WHEW, to much typing.<P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fsrowsell||09-07-2001||09:16 PM||||On my last Fiero/328 Kit. I cut the front 2 coils and also cut 2" off the bump stops, so she wouldn't bottom out on me. The handling was great...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||09-07-2001||09:24 PM||||On my 88GT, the rears are Fiero Store lowering springs, the fronts are stock with 1 complete coil cut from them. The front is probably about 1/2 inch higher than the rear, but I ain't pulling it apart again to cut a quarter of a coil off.||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||09-07-2001||09:51 PM||||Al,<BR> The old Belltech springs were blue, so if they haven't just been repainted, that's probably what they are. They are good for a 2" drop. Be sure to chech that car for the 2" Belltech drop spindles on the front too, they're quite valuable and no longer available. The spindles did not come with any paint and they look like factory parts so they are hard to spot.<P>Jon||||reg||1
Z||000008||rodmcneill||09-08-2001||07:42 AM||||When cutting front springs(88) does it make any difference if you cut from top or bottom?||||reg||1
Z||000009||MrPBody||09-08-2001||12:58 PM||||Oh, wait -- you <I>did</I> describe your handling problems:<P><B>Unpredictable</B> -- sounds like worn parts (ball joints, tie rod ends, or bushings) or mis-alignment.<P><B>Bouncy</B> -- sounds like worn shocks/struts<P><I>Edited for typo</I><P><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||09-08-2001||10:45 PM||||Eibach made blue springs. Im not sure if they make them anymore, I would think so though. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Alex4mula||09-09-2001||09:10 PM||||Hey California Kid;<BR> How much did you cut front and back to get that drop on your 88?? TIA<P><BR>V8 Dreamer; 2 & 1.5 coils??? Wow! That's a lot. I gess it's slammed now. Any pic?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||09-10-2001||09:57 AM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000013||V8Dreamer||09-10-2001||01:01 PM||||Yeah, it was quite a drop, you can only fit about a finger in the front, and there's maybe 1.75" gap in the rear(with 205/60/15 tires)......I don't have any pics currently, but I might be able to take one tonight.  Thanks for all of your responses guys, and FYI, as of now I'm thinking of putting suspension techniques lowering springs on the front so I can lighten up on the "pogo stick" effect I have right now.  I don't know if that's my whole problem, but I think it'll definately help.  <P>Ryan||||reg||1
